{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/82574-victorian-geist","id":82574,"title":"Victorian Geist","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-02T03:25:24-08:00","id":82574,"title":"Victorian Geist","content":"So I'm loosely rolling the idea around of running a game set in Victorian London, probably in the 1880s-1890s. I don't have too much trouble coming up with central plots, plus I foresee the group largely making their own stories, which I can facilitate without too much trouble.<br /> <br /> What I'm falling down on is sources on what it would be like to live there. Obviously it'd vary hugely on class and area. I can find stats, history, maps and so on easily enough (although if anyone has any really good sources on those it'd be nice). What I can't find is something that'd help me understand the day to day existence, struggles, victories of people in the area at the time.<br /> <br /> Anyone got any sources for that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T05:54:56-08:00","id":82594,"title":"","content":"There's a Changeling book called Victorian Lost that moght help you, and oWoD had a brief Victorian Vampire line. Both cover the setting well and could be a grand help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T06:06:21-08:00","id":82597,"title":"","content":"My advice, read Charles Dickens (disclaimer, I haven't).<br /> <br /> Basing a Victorian story on a masterpiece of Victorian storytelling is probably gong to be easier than basing it on a history book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T09:39:37-08:00","id":82672,"title":"","content":"You might want to try reading or watching an adaptation of Sherlock Holmes. It's the right era and it mixes low and high society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T12:52:46-08:00","id":82744,"title":"","content":"I recommend the Granada Television version of Sherlock Holmes, with Jeremy Brett. It is often on instant watch on Netflix. I am not positive if it is right at the moment but it often is. It's a damn good series, set in London (usually) very entertaining. Most of the &quot;movies&quot; are less good, being overly padded out (exception: Hound of the Baskervilles and Sign of Four, which are good) but the Adventures of Sherlock Holmes TV series is solid, though the last season suffers from Jeremy's ill health. They are very entertaining to watch, and have been some of my favorites my entire life.<br /> <br /> Comme Il Fault is a supplement for Castle Falkenstein written to introduce people to the victorian era. While it is written in CF's odd fiction system where someone from the present is supposedly sending you stuff from that setting, and it is set in CF's setting, it nonetheless has some very useful information. If you can find it sitting around inexpensively pick it up. I always use it for any Victorian set game, not just CF.<br /> <br /> Vampire (Masquerade) and Changeling (Lost) have Victorian set books, though they focus more on the game and how it is different for the setting than the setting itself. Still, if you have any of them sitting around they are good, and if you are into either setting they may be good for a game of that type someday.<br /> <br /> ETA: The Sherlock Holms are not on instant watch right now, but will be in the future I am sure. <a href=\"http://dvd.netflix.com/Movie/The-Adventures-of-Sherlock-Holmes/70142435?strkid=1424031231_0_0&amp;strackid=5efbb26f88b42f05_0_srl&amp;trkid=222336\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a> is the series, and the two good full length movies <a href=\"http://dvd.netflix.com/Movie/Sherlock-Holmes-The-Sign-of-Four/60026420?strkid=1525095925_0_0&amp;strackid=2e0a8d6ae0811ade_0_srl&amp;trkid=222336\" target=\"_blank\">The Sign of Four</a>, <a href=\"http://dvd.netflix.com/Movie/Sherlock-Holmes-The-Hound-of-the-Baskervilles/60026167?strkid=467397004_11_1&amp;strackid=42502ecf41370c2b_11_srl&amp;trkid=496833\" target=\"_blank\">The Hound of the Baskervilles</a>Even if you don't use Netflix this gives you the series covers to look for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 03-02-2014, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T17:55:36-08:00","id":82864,"title":"","content":"The corebook for the Unhallowed Metropolis game contains a fairly large amount of setting information on Victorian London as well. A lot of it has then been expanded to meet the game's 2105 setting, but as a rule the setting hasn't advanced all that much socially and a lot of what you read should be applicable. The history section also shows the roots of the game's setting, and in doing so provides a pretty good background on Victorian England in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T13:55:22-08:00","id":83444,"title":"","content":"<i>Daily Life in Victorian England</i> (1993) by Sally Mitchell seems good, read through a bit of it and skimmed the rest on Google Books (books.google.com). ISBN: 0313294674<br /> Also, more recently <i>Inside the Victorian Home: A Portrait of Domestic Life in Victorian England</i> (2003) by Judith Flanders seems like more recent information closer to what would be useful for a game setting. ISBN: 0393052095<br /> Whether or not these books are able to be purchased or even found... well, I can't do <i>all</i> the work. :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>ST/DM for <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCfFy7kNgMvxIR1qdzT8PzEg\" target=\"_blank\">Dice Alternatives</a><br /> Playing: <a href=\"http://causality-and-consequences.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">DtD: Causality and Consequence</a><br /> Off-Season: <a href=\"http://lifelong-educations.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">M:tAw- Lifelong Education</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/667-abenniton","name":"ABenniton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar667_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T18:35:06-08:00","id":83660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ABenniton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/82574-victorian-geist?p=83444#post83444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Daily Life in Victorian England</i> (1993) by Sally Mitchell seems good, read through a bit of it and skimmed the rest on Google Books (books.google.com). ISBN: 0313294674<br /> Also, more recently <i>Inside the Victorian Home: A Portrait of Domestic Life in Victorian England</i> (2003) by Judith Flanders seems like more recent information closer to what would be useful for a game setting. ISBN: 0393052095<br /> Whether or not these books are able to be purchased or even found... well, I can't do <i>all</i> the work. :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they can be found. Mitchell's work sells for about $70-$80, while Flanders' goes for more like $25. Better, to be sure, but you can understand I'm reluctant to drop money (and time, often takes upwards of a month for these to arrive since I'm usually ordering from overseas, or the store is from their supplier) on a book that reads well on Google Books. Hence I'm really looking for sources that people themselves have read, used and found helpful.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the tip, though.<br /> <br /> And thanks everyone else for your help so far <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Keep 'em coming though, if you think of something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T11:44:23-07:00","id":107580,"title":"","content":"It's a month late, but I, too, have been planning a Victorian game of Geist. I found Liza Picard's <i>Victorian London: The Tale of a City 1840-1870</i> at my library and it's been a huge help.<br /> <br /> Granted, I'm setting my game in 1888, but it's still a great source.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2660-gaeth","name":"Gaeth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T12:09:40-07:00","id":107596,"title":"","content":"If you guys do APs be sure and link them here. I want to read them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T12:29:03-07:00","id":107606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/82574-victorian-geist?p=107596#post107596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you guys do APs be sure and link them here. I want to read them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Might actually be doing an AP podcast. We'll see. I've got some time before it begins, though (currently the people who are interested in playing and I want in the game have no free day in common with each other. In a month or two that'll probably change as a werewolf game that they're all in ends)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2660-gaeth","name":"Gaeth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T17:31:15-07:00","id":107795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/82574-victorian-geist?p=107580#post107580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a month late, but I, too, have been planning a Victorian game of Geist. I found Liza Picard's <i>Victorian London: The Tale of a City 1840-1870</i> at my library and it's been a huge help.<br /> <br /> Granted, I'm setting my game in 1888, but it's still a great source.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. This game won't happen for at least a couple months, so no matter how late it seems, info is always good. If nothing else someone else might need it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T18:53:14-07:00","id":107857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/82574-victorian-geist?p=82744#post82744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recommend the Granada Television version of Sherlock Holmes, with Jeremy Brett. It is often on instant watch on Netflix. I am not positive if it is right at the moment but it often is. It's a damn good series, set in London (usually) very entertaining. Most of the &quot;movies&quot; are less good, being overly padded out (exception: Hound of the Baskervilles and Sign of Four, which are good) but the Adventures of Sherlock Holmes TV series is solid, though the last season suffers from Jeremy's ill health. They are very entertaining to watch, and have been some of my favorites my entire life.<br /> <br /> Comme Il Fault is a supplement for Castle Falkenstein written to introduce people to the victorian era. While it is written in CF's odd fiction system where someone from the present is supposedly sending you stuff from that setting, and it is set in CF's setting, it nonetheless has some very useful information. If you can find it sitting around inexpensively pick it up. I always use it for any Victorian set game, not just CF.<br /> <br /> Vampire (Masquerade) and Changeling (Lost) have Victorian set books, though they focus more on the game and how it is different for the setting than the setting itself. Still, if you have any of them sitting around they are good, and if you are into either setting they may be good for a game of that type someday.<br /> <br /> ETA: The Sherlock Holms are not on instant watch right now, but will be in the future I am sure. <a href=\"http://dvd.netflix.com/Movie/The-Adventures-of-Sherlock-Holmes/70142435?strkid=1424031231_0_0&amp;strackid=5efbb26f88b42f05_0_srl&amp;trkid=222336\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a> is the series, and the two good full length movies <a href=\"http://dvd.netflix.com/Movie/Sherlock-Holmes-The-Sign-of-Four/60026420?strkid=1525095925_0_0&amp;strackid=2e0a8d6ae0811ade_0_srl&amp;trkid=222336\" target=\"_blank\">The Sign of Four</a>, <a href=\"http://dvd.netflix.com/Movie/Sherlock-Holmes-The-Hound-of-the-Baskervilles/60026167?strkid=467397004_11_1&amp;strackid=42502ecf41370c2b_11_srl&amp;trkid=496833\" target=\"_blank\">The Hound of the Baskervilles</a>Even if you don't use Netflix this gives you the series covers to look for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find Ripper Street to be a good, if sometimes uneven, show with a relevant setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1966-jeffjerwin","name":"Jeffjerwin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T04:01:55-07:00","id":108080,"title":"","content":"Ripper Street is also on Netflix and BBCA On Demand if those help. And I agree, Ripper Street is a fair showing. The good, the bad, the ugly, and the nasty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is just my bright, shiny two cents.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing. I try not to argue in forums. It's like pouring concrete in a river. It doesn't get you anywhere in the short term and it poisons the environment long term.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2668-asmenedas","name":"Asmenedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2668_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T17:06:51-07:00","id":108785,"title":"","content":"I'll give it a look, thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><b